{"ts": "2026-08-26T04:23:55.255433+00:00", "event": "run_start", "task": "Whence in 12 lines (read SPEC.md with read_file for the full language):\n  let x = 1 + 2                # bind once; same-block rebinding is a parse error\n  fn f(a, b) { a * b }         # last expression is the value; tail calls loop\n  if c { 1 } else { 2 }        # if is an expression; non-bool condition -> miss\n  check \"label\": expr          # test statement, records ok/fail\n  print(x)  print(why x)       # why x = the provenance (why-tree) of x\n  miss \"reason\"                # every runtime error is a propagating `miss`\n  (expr rescue fallback)       # recover from a miss\n  [1, 2] @{k: 1}  xs[0] r.k    # lists, records, index, field\n  snip x  note(\"lbl\", x)       # cut / annotate provenance\n  builtins: len range map filter fold push str num abs sqrt missed reasons\n            contains join keys merge steps at blame diverge contrast\nValues ARE provenance nodes: `why`, `steps(x)`, `at(x, \"let a\")`,\n`diverge(a, b)`, `contrast(a, b)` inspect history and are part of behaviour.\n\nThe test suite of this Whence checkout fails. Output of `pytest -x -q tests`:\n```\nF\n=================================== FAILURES ===================================\n__________________________________ test_hello __________________________________\n\n    def test_hello():\n        r = run_example(\"hello.lang\")\n>       assert r.returncode == 0\nE       assert 1 == 0\nE        +  where 1 = CompletedProcess(args=['/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/usr/bin/python3', '/private/var/folders/_6/3xh6ssk928jcqvp...(line 7)\\n│        └─ 50 ← literal  (line 15)\\n└─ \"big\" ← literal  (line 19)\\nchecks: 0 passed, 2 failed\\n', stderr='').returncode\n\ntests/test_examples.py:21: AssertionError\n=========================== short test summary info ============================\nFAILED tests/test_examples.py::test_hello - assert 1 == 0\n!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! stopping after 1 failures !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n1 failed in 0.46s\n```\nThe tests are correct. Find the defect in whence/*.py and fix it with the smallest change that restores the intended semantics (edit_file replaces one exact occurrence). Do NOT edit anything under tests/. You have 20 tool steps in total; pytest on the whole suite takes 1-3 minutes, so run it at most three times.\noutline/read_file/search share a hard budget of 30 calls; after that they refuse.\nReading code: outline a file, then read_file with start/end (200-line windows); search takes a file or directory plus a context count; whence_run and oracle_check execute Whence programs against the CURRENT state of the checkout copy. Verify with pytest (args default to '-q tests').\nFinish with a JSON block:\n```json\n{\"root_cause\": \"...\", \"files\": [\"whence/interp.py\"], \"summary\": \"...\"}\n```", "tools": ["outline", "read_file", "search", "edit_file", "pytest", "whence_run", "oracle_check"], "max_steps": 20, "model": "claude-sonnet-5"}
